        "message": "Stage 1: design primitives\n\nSix primitives the system was missing. Measured across 58 screens: 1 had\na chart, none had a table, and 12 primitives were used over 2,000 times,\nso every screen rendered as cards of form fields whatever its job.\n\nStat is always a link — onOpen is required and a Stat without one refuses\nto render rather than shipping a dead figure, which was the most common\ndefect found in the review.\n\nQueueRow puts age first, coloured by wait, with byOldest() so a queue can\nonly be sorted the way that surfaces the problem. Actions inline.\n\nChart is inline SVG — line, bar, pairedBar, donut. No charting library:\nnone are small and all bring a visual opinion that fights this system,\nand the bundle is already over 1MB. Every chart carries a chart/table\ntoggle, since some people read shapes and others read numbers.\n\nTable sorts, exports CSV, and scrolls inside its own container so the\npage body never scrolls sideways on a phone.\n\nIcon is inline SVG, one weight, meaning not decoration. MapPin uses a\nstatic OpenStreetMap embed — no library, no key, no tracking of the\nviewer.\n\nTokens: contrast raised throughout and --act defined as the single colour\nmeaning act on this. The old palette put a muted green button on a\nnear-white card and it was invisible on the Assign screen.\n\nDemonstration route added at Primitives, loading live CEAC data. Nothing\nplaceholder: a primitive proved with invented numbers is not proved.\n\nNo existing screen changed.",
